@WillRapier A) the radioactive material is stored in safe facilities, and even then, that waste is not really that harmful, and after a few decades, it's not harmful at all. 

B) radioactive water is not dumped into nearby rivers. This isn't Russia. We have standards in the US. 

Nuclear energy is extremely cheap and energy dense, and far, far safer for the environment than anything else, including wind and solar
